  "approximated": true,
  "notes": "Values at the 3rd, 5th, 10th, 25th and 50th percentiles (indices 0-4 in the 'values' array) are transcribed verbatim from Table VI (boys) and Table VII (girls) of the published paper, at half-year resolution from 5.0 to 18.0 years (approximated=false for these). IMPORTANT: the paper does NOT publish 75th, 90th, 95th or 97th BMI percentiles \u2014 for BMI it instead publishes IOTF-style age-varying 'adult-equivalent' cut-off lines (BMI value that projects to adult BMI 23 and 27 kg/m^2), which are risk thresholds, not fixed percentiles, and were NOT used here. Instead, the 75th/90th/95th/97th percentiles (indices 5-8) were ESTIMATED per age/sex by fitting a Cole's LMS (Box-Cox) curve to the four known published points (3rd,5th,10th,25th) plus the median as M, via least-squares grid search over L (S solved by linear regression for each trial L), then extrapolating that fitted curve to the 75th/90th/95th/97th percentiles. This extrapolation is a modeled approximation beyond the range of directly published data and has NOT been validated against IAP's own (unpublished) LMS parameters. It should be independently verified by the clinic doctor before clinical use, especially for identifying overweight/obesity where IAP's own recommended method is the 23/27 adult-equivalent cut-off lines from Table VI/VII, not a 90th/95th percentile cut-off.",
